{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a", "label": "Web UI milestone UI-3a Implementation Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_22_mini_app_design", "label": "Mini App design spec (Advanced setup, Pages, Architecture, Testing, Milestones)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_configedit", "label": "dispatch.config.ConfigEdit (in-place YAML edits)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ruling 1: saving edits the YAML text in place using SnakeYAML node marks (set/remove/append) so only changed lines change, preserving comments, order and spacing; the file is replaced only through ConfigFile.replace (validate, then atomic move). This supersedes the original spec's 'rewrite the whole file' approach and its warning that comments will be lost. A flow-style collection ({...} or [...]) is refused with a message rather than edited, since editing inside one in place is error-prone."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_configtext", "label": "dispatch.config.ConfigText (visibility opened for ConfigEdit)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_config_runlimits_parseduration", "label": "Config.RunLimits.parseDuration (made public)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_setup_advanced", "label": "Setup.Advanced record + defaults-diff render", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Setup.render writes only what differs from today's defaults (plan 15m/$2, execute 60m/$10, 1 or 2 concurrent runs, default state dir, gh), so a quick setup renders the exact same config bytes it always has; every Advanced field left null keeps its default, verified by a test that Advanced answers equal to the defaults render the identical quick layout."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_cli_init_advanced", "label": "Cli.Init(configFile, force, advanced) / --advanced switch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_initcommand_advanced", "label": "InitCommand advanced questions (per-project + Advanced step)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ruling 3: dispatch init asks the Advanced questions (alias, per-phase model/effort, limits, concurrency, state directory, gh command) only with --advanced; InitCommandTest (the quick-setup contract) passes unchanged, and the web setup's Advanced section is likewise a closed panel by default."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_service_restart", "label": "Service.restart() default method", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ruling 4: default implementation is stop() then start(); a service manager with a native one-step restart (systemd) overrides it. launchd and Task Scheduler restart by stop-then-start too (bootout+bootstrap, /End+/Run), since only systemd has a genuine one-step restart worth overriding."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_systemdservice_restart", "label": "SystemdService.restart() override", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_manageapi", "label": "dispatch.ui.ManageApi (management reads/saves, logs, restart)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every management read answers 'version': the config file's SHA-256; every save sends it back, and a mismatch answers 409 changed ('the config changed on disk since this page loaded it; reload to see the change') - stale-edit detection is stateless, keyed purely on the file hash. Each save keeps dispatch.yaml.bak (the previous exact bytes, with the config's own POSIX permissions) written just before the validated ConfigFile.replace, so an aborted validation still leaves a harmless backup equal to the unchanged file. Unchanged values are never rewritten (e.g. 60m stays 60m although the page shows it as 1h). Removing a member also drops them from telegram.admins when no longer in any group, refused if it would leave no admin or leave a group empty; removing a project is refused if it is the last project or the only project of its group. Reading the service log uses a 'ponytail: only the log's last 1 MiB is read' shortcut (TAIL_BYTES), so a narrow filter can find fewer lines than asked; the stated upgrade path is reading further back in chunks if that matters. Restart (/api/service/restart) is refused with 400 when no service is installed."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_overviewapi_serviceview", "label": "OverviewApi.serviceView(Service) (shared service status view)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_usepath", "label": "usePath hook (path + navigate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ruling 5: no router dependency. usePath() is built directly over window.location.pathname, history.pushState and the popstate event, since UiServer already answers index.html for every extensionless page path (/, /projects, /people, /settings, /logs)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_userestart", "label": "useRestart hook (restart with polling)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Posts /api/service/restart, then polls the Overview every intervalMs (default 2s) for up to timeoutMs (default 60s) until the service reports running again; a lost connection during that window is expected and swallowed. After the timeout it gives up, fetches the service log's last 20 lines, and reports failed with a message naming how long it waited."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_restartnotice", "label": "RestartNotice / RestartStatus components", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shown after any management save: 'Saved. Restart to apply' with a Restart now button when the service is installed, because the running Dispatch only reads its config when it starts."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_usemanagedconfig", "label": "useManagedConfig hook (load + versioned save)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_managedpage", "label": "ManagedPage component (shared load/save/restart frame)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_settingspage", "label": "SettingsPage component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_projectform", "label": "ProjectForm component (shared add/edit project form)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_projectspage", "label": "ProjectsPage component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_peoplepage", "label": "PeoplePage component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_logspage", "label": "LogsPage component (self-polling log viewer)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asks /api/manage/logs again intervalMs (default 2s) after each answer, with the chosen level/event filter, only while the page is mounted; the polling loop self-schedules its own setTimeout rather than using a fixed interval, and stops cleanly on unmount."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_options_ts", "label": "options.ts (MODELS/EFFORTS/PHASE_MODELS/PHASE_EFFORTS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_playwright_e2e", "label": "Playwright end-to-end suite (ui/e2e/*) against the real dispatch ui jar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only new dependency (@playwright/test, dev-only, never bundled into the jar) permitted for UI-3a, because the spec requires real browser end-to-end tests and nothing already installed drives a real browser. The global setup starts the -Pui jar with a team config and two clones and logs the browser in once via the printed one-time link; the setup e2e test answers Telegram-facing calls with page.route since a release jar always talks to api.telegram.org and a fake token cannot pass getMe."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a", "target": "adr_0015", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_22_mini_app_design", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_22_web_ui_design", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_manageapi", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_configedit", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_configedit", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_configtext", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-22-web-ui-3a.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_3a_manageapi", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_22_web_ui_2_setupapi", "relation": "conceptually_relate